  "question": {
    "text": "A metal wire of resistance <math><mn>3</mn><mtext> </mtext><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Ω</mi></math> is elongated to make a uniform wire of double its previous length. This new wire is now bent and the ends joined to make a circle. If two points on this circle make an angle <math><msup><mrow><mn>60</mn></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi></mrow></msup></math> at the center, the equivalent resistance between these two points will be:"
